[QA 1] The paper introduces the first non-trivial update/query tradeoff for maintaining exact shortest paths in sparse weighted directed graphs, achieving polynomially better update/query bounds than previous randomized approaches while handling real-edge-weighted graphs deterministically. | The key contribution of the paper "Fully Dynamic Shortest Paths in Sparse Digraphs" is presenting the first fully dynamic all-pairs shortest paths data structure with non-trivial update and query time bounds for sparse weighted directed graphs, achieving an amortized update time of O(mn^4/5) and query time of O(n^4/5), where m is the number of edges and n is the number of vertices.
